+
+Add Browserbase in two packages: `effect-browserbase` owns one strict Client, session/context/extension resources, E/R-preserving typed bootstrap bindings, document readiness, scoped owned or borrowed browser operations, bounded capture, file selection and provider artifacts, with no Effect Agent dependency. `effect-agent-browserbase` adds the actual Effect Agent adapter and fixed Toolkit, including adaptation of the exact generic owner with shared connection, action and capture accounting, with no Playwright peer. Superseded constructors, subpaths, aliases and reexports are removed; maintained consumers use only the canonical packages.
