+### Browserbase interactive sessions
+
+`effect-agent-browserbase` implements the same `InteractiveBrowser` contract on trusted
+Node and Bun hosts with Playwright 1.63 over Browserbase CDP. One enclosing Scope owns the remote
+session; application code and model Tools borrow handles from that owner. Provider credentials,
+CDP addresses, persistent-context choices and Live View controls remain host-only.
+
+Browserbase currently supports only a trusted-host `Unrestricted` network policy in this adapter.
+`ExactHosts` fails before allocation because Browserbase `allowedDomains` does not prove exact-host
+coverage for redirects, frames, subresources, popups and service workers. `PublicWeb` also fails
+before allocation because request interception cannot establish connection-time public-address
+containment. Neither mode silently falls back to `Unrestricted`.
+
+The generic `effect-browserbase` package owns independent `recordings`, `replays`, and
+`downloads` entry points. Provider MP4 assembly and replay retrieval can outlive the interactive
+Scope; signed media URLs are temporary access material rather than artifact identity. Its optional
+`capture` borrows an owned page and streams bounded JPEG frames with source/receipt clocks and drop
+accounting. It owns no encoder or filesystem and does not claim website-audio capture. The adapter
+exports only its actual `adapter` and `tools` entry points, not generic or legacy reexports.
+
+Acquire typed initialization with `browser.withBrowser(policy, { bootstrap }, use)` or explicit
+`browser.open(policy, { bootstrap })`. `Bootstrap.binding` preserves consumer errors and services,
+admits finite work before spawning a scoped callback, and checks the native caller's origin and
+document identity before decoding, before running the handler and before replying. Fail-session
+callbacks supervise `withBrowser`; page-visible rejections never contain host causes or stacks.
+Use `fromSession(session)` from the adapter to give the fixed Toolkit that exact generic owner,
+with the same connection, action budget and capture accounting, rather than opening another one.
+
+Host handoff pauses automation before returning temporary Live View material. Resume requires an
+explicit operator-release decision and obtains a fresh observation while retaining the mutation
+permit. Keep-alive reconnect creates a new handle generation and never replays a pending mutation.
+Persistent writers require an application-owned exclusive context lease.
+
